                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c6179891-8922-3ced-ac58-5c613bccf76f",
                        "entry_id": "ba99933a-82aa-3494-9578-bf17fa7d5b7e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete spelling of loss."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ffee494-acbf-4ee7-91e5-0e4e158dd4e4",
                                "sense_id": "c6179891-8922-3ced-ac58-5c613bccf76f",
                                "text": "Who dyes the vtmoſt dolor doth abye, / But who that liues, is lefte to waile his loſſe: / So life is loſſe, and death felicity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b7cba9e-1d36-4298-8197-ca17bd6c2a87",
                                "sense_id": "c6179891-8922-3ced-ac58-5c613bccf76f",
                                "text": "Then way what loſſe your honor may ſuſtaine / If with too credent eare you liſt his ſongs / Or looſe your hart, or your chaſt treaſure open / To his vnmaſtred importunity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af7115be-60d7-469b-96cc-947708783454",
                                "sense_id": "c6179891-8922-3ced-ac58-5c613bccf76f",
                                "text": "[…]the Lord denounceth thoſe iudgements againſt her, from which ſpecially ſhee bleſſed her ſelfe, euen loſſe of Soueraigntie, ſlaughter and deſolation :[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93cda28d-2acc-4208-9605-2ce48076c088",
                                "sense_id": "c6179891-8922-3ced-ac58-5c613bccf76f",
                                "text": "Soe they resolved with losse of their lives to recover or to end the losse of theire libertie , being overcarried indifferently with hate and disdaine , two mightie passions to drive on disordered desires"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
